probe.tightened_rule:
Name: Result rows cite the reviewed head.

Trigger (PR body only, never source files): a sentence or table row in the body that reports a MEASUREMENT of the PR's code: unit-test outcome or assertion count, token identity, perf A/B numbers, objdump/instruction comparison, lint rc, build rc. A sentence that names a commit for what it changed ('commit X removes ...', 'merge commit X', 'the head the review was made on') is not a measurement and is skipped, wherever it stands. Short-version summaries, pass-rule definitions and reference bands from outside the PR (for example 'reference spread measured on 2026-09-14') are not rows.

Setup: HEAD = `gh pr view N --json headRefOid`; BASE = `git merge-base $HEAD origin/main` (never the cited id's merge-base); PRFILES = `git diff --name-only $BASE $HEAD`. Candidate ids: hex of 7-40 chars whose `git cat-file -t` prints exactly `commit` (drops GitHub comment numbers and numeric literals such as 00006103515625f). For each id: ANCESTOR via `git merge-base --is-ancestor ID $HEAD`; BEHIND = rev-list count if ancestor, else 'not an ancestor (amended/rebased/squashed)'; CHANGED = PRFILES whose content differs between ID and HEAD.

Finding conditions, one per result kind:
(a) the row cites an id != HEAD and carries no label (pre-merge, pre-rebase, scheduled) -> finding;
(b) the row cites an id != HEAD with a label but says neither which PR files are unchanged between the two (CHANGED empty, or the test binary compiles none of CHANGED) nor when the re-run happens, AND does not disclose a known difference -> finding; a label plus a stated limitation ('still had the placement-new pass') is accepted, the only ask is to add the id;
(c) a row with no id of its own inherits the id of the nearest 'Binary:' line in the same section; flag 'no provenance' only when no such line exists in the section;
(d) present-tense wording ('ran at the head X', 'now X', 'current X') around an id != HEAD -> finding; past tense is not flagged;
(e) baseline check (cited main id != BASE) only for rows whose own id == HEAD; a row already flagged under (a) or (b) is not flagged again for its baseline;
(f) date comparison only for rows with no id at all, and only when the row has a time of day or is dated before the head commit's calendar day.

Ask per kind: unit tests, token identity, lint, build -> re-run at HEAD, or delete when rows at HEAD already exist below, or label with the reason; perf A/B and objdump -> label with the id (re-run is not demanded by this rule); assertion-count arithmetic between two old ids -> defer to the prose rule (delete), not re-run.

Guards: an id equal to HEAD; ids inside the Commits or review-thread tables; a 'now'/'the head' sentence in the past tense; a labelled row that states its scope or its limitation; rows re-run at HEAD with unchanged numbers; the baseline of an already-flagged row; dates without time on the head commit's day.

Finding template (two sentences, Wade's form): 'PR description, <section>: the <kind> rows cite <id>, <BEHIND> behind the head <HEAD>; the merge of main changed <CHANGED> since then[, and line <n> calls <id> "the head"]. Please <re-run them at <HEAD> | delete them, the rows at <HEAD> below replace them | mark them pre-merge and say which files did not change>.'

